`r[p[i]] = q[i]`

In permutation composition terms, this is equivalent to:

`r = q ∘ p⁻¹`  
or more directly:  
`r = p` applied to indices of `q`.

We can simulate the recurrence using fast exponentiation of a linear transformation in the permutation group.  

